From eb8a60761746db16f20d26fe953340daac9d48c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nsbradley88 <3960699+nsbradley88@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:33:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/23] vulkan: fuse RMS_NORM + SCALE and SCALE -> SIGMOID ->
 SCALE

- RMS_NORM_SCALE: rms_norm(x)*c (no bias) as one dispatch; the factor goes in
  the rms_norm param2 (both the plain and the partials shader). This is the GDN
  l2 norm (build_gdn_l2_norm), -68 dispatches per glm5-next graph.
- SCALE_SIGMOID_SCALE: s_out*sigmoid(s_in*x) (no biases) as one unary
  dispatch, the KDA decay gate lb*sigmoid(-A*g), -68 per graph.
- Both evaluate the same f32 operations in the same order as the unfused ops.
- graph_optimize keeps both pairs adjacent (RMS_NORM -> SCALE like
  RMS_NORM -> MUL; SCALE/SIGMOID/SCALE as a kept pattern).
- test-backend-ops: RMS_NORM_SCALE, SCALE_SIGMOID_SCALE whole-graph cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
